# Phase 5 EOL policy decision (P5 Task 7 — finalizes the "revisit" this file used to defer).
# Broadened from `*.svelte` alone to every text extension this migration actually authors,
# proven a content no-op by a node Buffer (byte 13) CR scan over every tracked file's INDEX
# blob (`git ls-files -s` -> `git cat-file -p` per sha; the worktree is not authoritative here
# — see below) BEFORE this rule was added: 170 .svelte / 130 .ts / 5 .js / 5 .css / 1 .scss /
# 1 .html tracked files, zero CR bytes in any of them.
#
# `*.json` is deliberately NOT added: of 410 tracked files across these 9 candidate extensions,
# the same index-blob scan found CR in exactly 3 — all .json, across two pre-migration
# directories: static/locales/ru.json, and test/inputs/example-composed.skysheet.json +
# test/inputs/example-recorded.skysheet.json — renormalizing them is out of scope for this
# task, and test/fixtures/ (immutable) is itself all .json, so a blanket json rule is the wrong
# shape of risk to take here. Revisit with a narrower, path-scoped rule if a future phase wants
# LF-locked JSON.
#
# `*.md` and `*.yml` are added with NO path carve-outs: the index-blob scan found zero CR in any
# tracked .md or .yml file, including static/assets/audio/sky/SFX_*/README.md (8 files),
# test-songs/ThingsToTest.md, and .github/FUNDING.yml — those 10 files are pure LF in the repo.
# (This checkout's worktree copies of them are locally CRLF-ified, a stale local artifact of
# this environment, not a repo fact — do not scan the worktree for this decision, only the
# index.) A `-text` carve-out on any of the 10 would disable normalization and let the next
# `git add` of that path commit its CRLF worktree bytes over the currently-LF index blob —
# exactly the damage a carve-out is meant to prevent — so none is applied.
#
# No blanket `* text=auto`: that would reclassify every binary/asset path under static/ and
# test/fixtures/ — fixtures are immutable.
*.svelte text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.scss text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
